{
  "requirement": "requirements.ci.errors",
  "file": "src/execution_coverage/check.rs",
  "item": "fn[exceptions]",
  "queries": [
    "early_exits",
    "error_accumulators"
  ],
  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/execution_coverage/check.rs#fn[exceptions]` takes a parameter named `errors` and is a repository-validation function that collects validation errors, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`. It meets the site obligations.\n\n- **`return Ok(BTreeMap::new())`:** This is reached only when `crate::evidence::load_definitions` fails. The function pushes that error into `errors` first. All the remaining work (`citation_items`, `HabeasDomain::new`, and the per-item `validate_review` calls) uses `definitions`, so it depends on the failed check's result. `collect_references` already ran before the failure and reported its own errors. The caller `src/execution_coverage/check.rs#fn[check_saved]` takes the empty map and carries on with `discovered_files`, inventory and the threshold checks, so the failure doesn't stop the wider run. This return does not skip any later independent check.\n- **`continue`:** This skips items that have no `habeas:coverage` citation. Nothing has failed for those items, so no check is skipped after a failure.\n- **Failures inside the loop:** For each cited item the function pushes either a missing-review finding or the `validate_review` findings. It then records the exception and calls `errors.extend(findings)`. A failure on one item does not stop later items from being checked.\n- **Duplicate reporting:** Each failure is pushed once. `fn[check_saved]` also dedupes `errors` before it reports them.\n- **Error format:** The messages that `fn[exceptions]` pushes begin with the affected path, name the failed check and give the remedy. This matches the `requirements.ci.validation_error` format.\n\nBoth violation matches are harmless here, and I found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/execution_coverage/check.rs",
      "item": "fn[exceptions]",
      "hash": "6e9ad89de2f027e7bda75b14b557fe7e10abecf524317a8d99499957470d8f95"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
